; An annotation is a list between a declaration's keyword and its name
; (`D-122`), and the names it may carry are a closed table. A misspelling is a
; refusal about the annotation rather than about the declaration under it,
; which is the whole reason the mechanism has a position of its own.
(fn (inlien) hot ((x i64)) -> i64 (* x x))

(fn main () -> i32 0)
